#: app/templates/main/security.html:8
msgid ""
"EcoBank exists so that people can take part in a community on the Hive "
"network without first becoming a blockchain expert. Here is exactly how that"
" works and where your keys are."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:10
msgid "Most people here hold no keys at all"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:11
msgid ""
"The common way to use EcoBank is to join a community and publish through the"
" account that community shares. You write, and the community's account "
"publishes it. You never see a key, never hold a key, and never need one. If "
"you leave, the community keeps its account and you keep your EcoBank login."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:13
msgid "This is the opposite of buying crypto"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:14
msgid ""
"You do not put money in and hold a balance. You get an account and earn over"
" time by taking part. Hive transactions are essentially free. The only thing"
" with a price on EcoBank is creating a brand-new Hive account (about 3 HIVE "
"of network cost, which EcoBank covers for you). Nobody funds a balance, buys"
" a token, or makes an investment here."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:16
msgid "If you do run your own digital profile"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:17
msgid ""
"Some people want their own Hive account. You can create one through EcoBank "
"or connect one you already have. In both cases EcoBank stores the keys it "
"needs, encrypted at rest, and decrypts them only to carry out an action you "
"asked for (publishing a post, or a wallet action you requested)."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:19
msgid "Profiles you connect"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:20
msgid ""
"You provide only the individual key(s) you choose to delegate, usually just "
"the posting key. EcoBank verifies each key against the account's on-chain "
"authorities and stores nothing else. It never asks for, receives, or stores "
"your master password or your owner key. If you only have a master password, "
"you derive the posting key yourself with an external tool and bring back "
"just that key."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:22
msgid "Profiles EcoBank creates for you"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:23
msgid ""
"For an account EcoBank creates, it keeps the master password, encrypted, on "
"purpose. A new account has no value, and beginners who are handed sole "
"responsibility for a key on day one routinely lose it and the account with "
"it. EcoBank holds the keys so that later, once the account has become worth "
"looking after, you can retrieve everything and take full control. You can "
"download a backup of your keys at any time, and remove the account from "
"EcoBank whenever you want; it stays valid on Hive."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:25
msgid "What each key can do"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:27
msgid ""
"Posting key: publish, comment, vote. Cannot touch funds. This is all EcoBank"
" needs to publish for you."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:28
msgid ""
"Active key: move funds and change account settings. EcoBank only stores this"
" if you explicitly add it for wallet actions."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:29
msgid "Memo key: read and write encrypted memos. Optional."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:30
msgid ""
"Owner key: full control, including recovery. EcoBank never accepts or stores"
" an owner key for a connected profile."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:33
msgid "EcoBank will never ask you for a key"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:34
msgid ""
"EcoBank will never email you, message you, or call you asking for a key, a "
"master password, or your EcoBank password. Anyone who does is impersonating "
"us. The only place you ever enter a key is the \"Connect a digital profile\""
" page on this site, over HTTPS, when you chose to go there."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:36
#, fuzzy
msgid "Reporting a problem"
msgstr "Error al actualizar el perfil."

#: app/templates/main/security.html:37
msgid "Security reports go to"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/security.html:37
msgid ""
"staffed by the SRBDE team. Please include steps to reproduce. We do not run "
"a paid bounty program, but we credit reporters who ask to be credited."
msgstr ""

