#: app/templates/main/terms.html:14
#, fuzzy
msgid "2. Your EcoBank account"
msgstr "Error cargando cuentas"

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:15
msgid ""
"You are responsible for keeping your EcoBank login secure and for activity "
"under it. Give us an address you can receive mail at. You must be old enough"
" to form a binding contract where you live. We may suspend or close accounts"
" that break these terms or are used for abuse."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:17
#, fuzzy
msgid "3. Circles and shared accounts"
msgstr "No se encontraron cuentas compartidas"

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:18
msgid ""
"A circle is a group of people who share one Hive account to publish "
"together. The circle's owner controls its membership and settings. If you "
"post through a circle's account, your post is published by that account and "
"is subject to the circle's rules. Leaving a circle does not remove content "
"you already published."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:20
msgid "4. Digital profiles and keys"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:21
msgid ""
"A digital profile is a Hive account. Its keys are yours. You can create a "
"profile through EcoBank or connect one you already have."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:23
msgid ""
"For a profile EcoBank creates, EcoBank keeps the keys (including the master "
"password) encrypted, so you can start taking part without managing them yet."
" You can download a backup at any time and take full control whenever you "
"want."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:24
msgid ""
"For a profile you connect, EcoBank stores only the individual key(s) you "
"choose to provide, and never your master password or owner key."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:25
msgid ""
"You can remove any profile from EcoBank at any time. The account stays valid"
" on Hive; EcoBank simply stops holding its keys and can no longer act for "
"it."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:27
msgid ""
"EcoBank keeps keys encrypted at rest and uses them only to carry out actions"
" you request. No system is perfectly secure; holding your own keys is always"
" the safest option, and EcoBank is built to hand them back."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:29
msgid "5. Credits and payment"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:30
msgid ""
"Creating a new Hive account has a small network cost (about 3 HIVE). A "
"credit is prepaid account creation: EcoBank covers that cost and does the "
"setup, and the credit price is the service fee. One credit creates one "
"profile."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:32
msgid ""
"The current price is shown on the credits page. Payments are processed by "
"PayPal under their terms; EcoBank does not store card details."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:33
msgid ""
"A credit is not currency, a token, a deposit, or an investment. It has no "
"cash value beyond its use to create one account, earns nothing, and cannot "
"be traded or transferred."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:34
msgid ""
"An unused credit can be refunded on request. Once a credit has been used to "
"create an account, it is non-refundable, because the network cost has been "
"spent."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:37
#, fuzzy
msgid "6. Content and the blockchain"
msgstr "Cuenta no encontrada en la blockchain Hive."

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:38
msgid ""
"Content you publish is written to the public Hive blockchain. It is public "
"and effectively permanent: EcoBank cannot edit or delete it once published, "
"and neither can anyone else. You are responsible for what you publish and "
"confirm you have the right to publish it. You keep ownership of your "
"content; you grant EcoBank permission to publish and display it as part of "
"running the service."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:39
msgid ""
"EcoBank sets itself as a beneficiary on posts it publishes, taking a share "
"of any author rewards those posts earn (currently 10%). This funds the "
"service. Hive author rewards are variable and are often zero; nothing here "
"is a promise of earnings."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:41
msgid "7. Acceptable use"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:42
msgid ""
"Do not use EcoBank to publish unlawful content, impersonate others, send "
"spam, infringe copyright, or attack the service or the Hive network. Do not "
"try to access accounts or data that are not yours."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:44
msgid "8. Not a financial service"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:45
msgid ""
"EcoBank does not take deposits, hold or transmit money, provide financial or"
" investment advice, or offer any return. HIVE, HIVE Power and HBD shown in a"
" wallet view belong to a Hive account you control and are governed by the "
"Hive network, not by EcoBank. Nothing on EcoBank is an offer to buy or sell "
"a security or currency."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:47
msgid "9. No warranty; limitation of liability"
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:48
#, python-format
msgid ""
"EcoBank is provided \"as is\", without warranties of any kind. We do not "
"guarantee the service will be uninterrupted or error-free, or that the Hive "
"network will behave in any particular way. To the extent the law allows, "
"%(entity)s and SRBDE are not liable for indirect or consequential losses, or"
" for loss of rewards, keys, or content beyond our reasonable control. "
"Nothing in these terms limits liability that cannot be limited by law."
msgstr ""

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:50
#, fuzzy
msgid "10. Changes"
msgstr "Cambios"

#: app/templates/main/terms.html:51
msgid ""
"We may update these terms. Material changes will be announced on the site. "
"Continuing to use EcoBank after a change means you accept the updated terms."
msgstr ""

